<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 56-day T-bills 99 pct sold, yield 50 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 56-day T-bills 99 pct sold, yield 50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 6.5 billion levs of 56-day floater coupon T-bills was 98.9 percent sold, yielding 50.36 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry for Monday's auction.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 300 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG 3018996028</p>
<p> Par value			 6.5 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		    October 7, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			October 9, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		   December 4, 1996</p>
<p> Bids received		   6,500 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	     96.15 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		   6,430 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	    97.12 levs</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   50.36 pct</p>
<p> Average annual yield	  328.22 pct</p>
<p> Cumulative annual yield     1,327.18 pct</p>
<p>-- Dessislava Popova, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-981 8569</p>
